          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures. Seizure onset occurred at 81 years of age. The current seizure frequency is approximately three seizures per week. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology due to a PCDH19 c.918G>A variant and is drug-resistant.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Valproate\n- Levetiracetam\n- Lamotrigine\n- Perampanel\n\nSeizure Burden:\nFocal impaired-awareness seizures occur approximately three times per week despite the current antiseizure medication regimen.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures, of genetic etiology associated with the causative PCDH19 c.918G>A variant.\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen of valproate, levetiracetam, lamotrigine, and perampanel.",
